## Ticket #4471: dates parse mm/dd in eu locales

Analysis of 427 reports merged into ticket #4471 revealed two distinct root causes for booking dates landing on the wrong day.

## Problems Found

### 1. Date Parser Bug
**Reports covered:** 393

The date parser reads all dates as MM/DD globally, but tenants in day-first locales write dates as DD/MM. This flips the day and month.

**Affected locales:** en-GB, nl-NL, cs-CZ, it-IT, and others with day-first formatting.

**GitHub issue:** [Date parser reads month-first in day-first locales](https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/7)

### 2. Booking-v3 Form Hint Bug
**Reports covered:** 34

The booking-v3 form displays "MM/DD/YYYY" hint in day-first locales. Users follow the hint and type month-first, but the form parser expects day-first input, causing another date flip.

**Affected locales:** Same day-first locales using booking-v3 form.

**GitHub issue:** [Booking-v3 form hint confuses date input in day-first locales](https://github.com/poponuts/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/8)

## Summary

Both issues stem from a mismatch between locale expectations and how dates are parsed or hinted:
- Parser bug: system always reads month-first
- Hint bug: form shows month-first hint but parser expects day-first

Total reports analyzed: 427 from April to October 2026.
